    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><anchor id="index_1md__i_1_2_falling_sand_2_r_e_a_d_m_e"/></para>
<para><bold>Falling Sand</bold> is a real-time <bold>2D falling-sand / cellular automata</bold> sandbox for Windows. You paint ten materials onto a <bold>384×224</bold> cell grid; <bold>granular solids</bold> fall, <bold>gases</bold> rise, <bold>liquids</bold> are solved with a GPU pressure–flux pipeline, and <bold>thermal chemistry</bold> drives fire, smoke, steam, melting, and quenching. The simulation and renderer run almost entirely on the <bold>Vulkan 1.3</bold> device via <bold>GLSL 460</bold> compute and graphics shaders; the host is <bold>C++23</bold> with a native <bold>Win32</bold> window and an immediate-mode pixel UI composited in a second draw pass.</para>
<para>Default startup scene is <bold>Thermal</bold> (<computeroutput>Scene::thermal</computeroutput>). The intro blurb in older docs referred to “Thermal Vent” — that preset matches <computeroutput>layouts/thermal.json</computeroutput>.</para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
