<sect1 id="index_1features">
<title>Features</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><bold>Ten paintable materials</bold> (sand, water, oil, stone, wood, fire, smoke, steam, lava, ice) plus empty cells for erase.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Four built-in scenes</bold> loaded from JSON (<computeroutput>waterworks</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>thermal</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>refinery</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>empty</computeroutput>).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>GPU simulation</bold> at <bold>90 Hz</bold> during play (fixed <computeroutput>simulationHz</computeroutput>), with pause and single-step.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Brush painting</bold>, <bold>erase</bold> (right mouse), and <bold>stir</bold> (middle mouse) implemented in <computeroutput>brush.comp</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Instanced HUD</bold>: material palette, scene tabs, transport controls, FPS/GPU badge, brush size track, pause/settings overlays (<computeroutput><ref refid="ui_8cpp_source" kindref="compound">ui.cpp</ref></computeroutput> → <computeroutput>ui.vert</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>ui.frag</computeroutput>).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Save/load</bold> of cell state to a binary sandbox file under <computeroutput>LOCALAPPDATA%\FallingSand\world.sandbox</computeroutput> (or current-directory fallback).</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="index_1requirements">
<title>Requirements</title><para><table rows="6" cols="2"><row>
<entry thead="yes"><para>Component  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Version / notes  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para>OS  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><bold>Windows x64</bold> only (<computeroutput>CMakeLists.txt</computeroutput> rejects non-Win32).  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para>CMake  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><bold>3.28+</bold>  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para>Compiler  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><bold>Visual Studio 2022</bold> (x64), C++23 (<computeroutput>/W4</computeroutput>, static MSVC runtime in Release)  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para>Vulkan  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><bold>1.3</bold> instance/device, <computeroutput>glslc</computeroutput> from the Vulkan SDK (<computeroutput>Vulkan::Vulkan</computeroutput> + <computeroutput>glslc</computeroutput> target)  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para>GPU  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Compute workgroups up to <bold>16×16</bold>, <bold>≥10</bold> storage buffers per stage, timestamp queries optional  </para>
</entry></row>
</table>
</para>
<para>Runtime: place <bold><computeroutput>FallingSand.exe</computeroutput></bold> next to copied <bold><computeroutput>shaders/</computeroutput></bold> (SPIR-V) and <bold><computeroutput>layouts/</computeroutput></bold> (JSON). CMake target <computeroutput>sand_shaders</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>sand_layouts</computeroutput> copy these into <computeroutput>build/&lt;Config&gt;/</computeroutput> automatically.</para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
</sect1>
