<para><computeroutput>makeScene</computeroutput> reads JSON beside the executable, validates dimensions, and fills a <computeroutput>worldCells</computeroutput> vector. Switching scenes from the UI <bold>replaces</bold> the grid (save first if you care about the current world).</para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="index_1save-format">
<title>Save format</title><para><computeroutput>saveWorld</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>loadWorld</computeroutput> (<computeroutput><ref refid="game_8cpp_source" kindref="compound">game.cpp</ref></computeroutput>):</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Magic: <bold><computeroutput>SAND0001</computeroutput></bold> (8 bytes).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>uint32_t</computeroutput> width, height — must match <computeroutput>worldWidth</computeroutput> (384) and <computeroutput>worldHeight</computeroutput> (224).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>worldCells</computeroutput> × <bold>16-byte <computeroutput>Cell</computeroutput></bold> records (trivially copyable, GPU-matched layout).</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Writes use a <computeroutput>.tmp</computeroutput> sibling file when possible. Load does not restore velocity or pressure; <computeroutput>VulkanGame::replaceWorld</computeroutput> uploads cells and <bold>zero-fills</bold> flow/auxiliary buffers (indices 2, 3, 5, 6 in storage).</para>
<para>Default path: <computeroutput>LOCALAPPDATA%\FallingSand\world.sandbox</computeroutput>, else <computeroutput>./world.sandbox</computeroutput> (<computeroutput>saveLocation()</computeroutput> in <computeroutput><ref refid="main_8cpp_source" kindref="compound">main.cpp</ref></computeroutput>).</para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="index_1data-model">
<title>Data model</title><sect2 id="index_1autotoc_md16">
<title><computeroutput>Cell</computeroutput> (CPU and GPU, 16 bytes)</title><para><programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="keyword">struct<sp/></highlight><highlight class="normal">Cell<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>std::array&lt;float,<sp/>3&gt;<sp/>liquid;<sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>x=water,<sp/>y=oil,<sp/>z=lava<sp/>—<sp/>fill<sp/>in<sp/>[0,<sp/>1]</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>std::uint32_t<sp/>matter;<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>packed<sp/>id,<sp/>age,<sp/>heat</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">};</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>Shader-side mirror in <computeroutput>world.glsl</computeroutput> (<computeroutput>vec3 liquid</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>uint matter</computeroutput>).</para>
</sect2>
<sect2 id="index_1autotoc_md17">
<title>Packed <computeroutput>matter</computeroutput> word</title><para><table rows="5" cols="3"><row>
<entry thead="yes"><para>Bits  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Field  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Access  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para>0–7  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Material id  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>material(c)</computeroutput> → <computeroutput>c.matter &amp; 255u</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para>8–15  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Age (e.g. smoke/fire lifetime)  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>age(c)</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para>16–25  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Heat (0…1023 → 0…1)  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>heat(c)</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para>(upper)  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Remaining bits unused in helpers  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>packMatter(id, life, temperature)</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry></row>
</table>
</para>
<para>Material constants (shader and logic): <computeroutput>EMPTY</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>SAND</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>WATER</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>OIL</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>STONE</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>WOOD</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>FIRE</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>SMOKE</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>STEAM</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>LAVA</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>ICE</computeroutput> (0–10).</para>
</sect2>
<sect2 id="index_1autotoc_md18">
<title>Liquids</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Three <bold>immiscible fill channels</bold> share one velocity field; <bold>separate.comp</bold> slowly exchanges oil/lava vs water between staggered row pairs.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>wet(c)</computeroutput> when total liquid <computeroutput>volume(c) &gt; 0.028</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Inverse density</bold> for pressure face weights uses channel weights <computeroutput>(1.0, 0.78, 2.3)</computeroutput> in <computeroutput>inverseDensity</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</sect2>
<sect2 id="index_1autotoc_md19">
<title>Solids and gases</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>solid(c)</computeroutput>: stone, wood, ice, sand — block face connections via <computeroutput>faceWeight</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>gas(id)</computeroutput>: fire, smoke, steam — handled in <bold>grains</bold> (rise) and <bold>reaction</bold>.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</sect2>
<sect2 id="index_1autotoc_md20">
<title>Host helpers</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>makeCell(Material, quantity)</computeroutput> — initial paint/scene values.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>displayMaterial</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>kind</computeroutput> — UI and tooltips from liquid + matter.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
</sect2>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="index_1gpu-buffers-and-ping-pong">
<title>GPU buffers and ping-pong</title><para>From <computeroutput>world.glsl</computeroutput> (compute; read-only subset in <computeroutput>world.frag</computeroutput> via <computeroutput>WORLD_READ_ONLY</computeroutput>):</para>
<para><table rows="8" cols="3"><row>
<entry thead="yes"><para>Binding  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Buffer  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Role  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para>0–1  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>CellsA</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>CellsB</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Cell ping-pong (<computeroutput>pc.state</computeroutput> selects read; writes use <computeroutput>writeCell</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>writeOther</computeroutput>)  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para>2  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>Velocity</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Staggered-style face flow used by flux/advect/project  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para>3  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>Prediction</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Predicted velocity (predict pass)  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para>4  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>Equations</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Pressure network row per cell (<computeroutput>Equation</computeroutput>: <computeroutput>vec4 weights</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>float rhs</computeroutput>)  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para>5–6  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>PressureA</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>PressureB</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Pressure ping-pong for Jacobi  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para>7  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>Flux</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Outward liquid flux per cell  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para>8–9  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>LimitA</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>LimitB</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Inflow capacity ping-pong for limit/advect  </para>
</entry></row>
</table>
</para>
<para><bold>Push constant <computeroutput>Frame</computeroutput></bold> (<computeroutput>world.glsl</computeroutput>): grid <computeroutput>size</computeroutput>, ping-pong <computeroutput>state</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>tick</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>operation</computeroutput> (<computeroutput>mode</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>phase</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>material</computeroutput>, spare), <computeroutput>brush</computeroutput> segment, <computeroutput>canvas</computeroutput> rect, <computeroutput>cursor</computeroutput> (world xy, radius, visibility), <computeroutput>screen</computeroutput> (width, height, visual time).</para>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="vulkan_8cpp_source" kindref="compound">vulkan.cpp</ref></computeroutput> constants:</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><bold><computeroutput>pressureBatches = 12</computeroutput></bold> — 12 pressure dispatches per tick (red-black <computeroutput>operation[1] = pass &amp; 1</computeroutput>).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold><computeroutput>fluxLimitPasses = 5</computeroutput></bold> — odd count so limit field settles before advection.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="index_1frame-pipeline-host">
<title>Frame pipeline (host)</title><para>Each frame (<computeroutput>VulkanGame::draw</computeroutput>):</para>
<para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Wait on frame-in-flight fence; optional timestamp readback.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Acquire swapchain image.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Upload <bold>UI quads</bold> to the slot’s storage buffer.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Compute</bold> (if stroke and/or <computeroutput>ticks &gt; 0</computeroutput>):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Optional <bold><computeroutput>brush.comp</computeroutput></bold> for the current stroke.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold><computeroutput>recordSim</computeroutput></bold>: <computeroutput>ticks</computeroutput> iterations of the simulation chain (below).</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Graphics</bold> (<computeroutput>recordDraw</computeroutput>):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Barrier: compute writes → fragment shader read.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Dynamic rendering: clear → <bold>world</bold> pass (scissored to canvas) → <bold>UI</bold> pass (full window).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Present (or capture BMP via transfer).</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para>Play loop (<computeroutput><ref refid="main_8cpp_source" kindref="compound">main.cpp</ref></computeroutput>): when not paused, accumulates real time and runs <computeroutput>floor(accumulator / tickSeconds)</computeroutput> ticks per frame (<computeroutput>tickSeconds = 1/90</computeroutput>). Paused runs 0 ticks unless <bold>N</bold> or UI <bold>step</bold> sets a one-shot tick. Benchmark/capture modes force <bold>1 tick/frame</bold>.</para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="index_1simulation-tick-compute">
<title>Simulation tick (compute)</title><para>Order inside <bold>one tick</bold> (<computeroutput>VulkanGame::Impl::recordSim</computeroutput> in <computeroutput><ref refid="vulkan_8cpp_source" kindref="compound">vulkan.cpp</ref></computeroutput>). Brush is <bold>outside</bold> this loop and runs once per frame when the user strokes.</para>
<para><table rows="13" cols="4"><row>
<entry thead="yes" align='right'><para>Step  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Kernel  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Workgroup layout  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>What it does  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no" align='right'><para>1  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><bold>reaction.comp</bold>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>16×8  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Chemistry: heat, fire, quenching, melting, smoke/steam lifetimes; updates <computeroutput>matter</computeroutput> and liquid mix.  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no" align='right'><para>—  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>state ^= 1</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>—  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Toggle cell buffer ping-pong.  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no" align='right'><para>2  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><bold>grains.comp</bold>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>16×8 over 2×2 blocks  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Sand <bold>falls</bold>, gas <bold>rises</bold>; local 2×2 updates to reduce races.  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no" align='right'><para>3  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><bold>predict.comp</bold>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>16×8  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Semi-Lagrangian <bold>velocity prediction</bold> from neighbors, viscosity, gravity.  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no" align='right'><para>4  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><bold>equation.comp</bold>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>16×8  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Build <bold>pressure network row</bold> per wet, non-solid cell (<computeroutput>faceWeight</computeroutput> on neighbors).  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no" align='right'><para>5  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><bold>pressure.comp</bold> ×12  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>16×16, shared mem  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><bold>Jacobi</bold> relaxation on pressure (two iterations per dispatch, halo tile); red-black phases via <computeroutput>operation[1]</computeroutput>.  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no" align='right'><para>6  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><bold>project.comp</bold>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>16×8  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><bold>Project</bold> predicted velocity with pressure gradients (divergence reduction).  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no" align='right'><para>7  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><bold>flux.comp</bold>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>16×8  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Face <bold>outward liquid flux</bold> from velocity; negative flow pulls from neighbors.  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no" align='right'><para>8  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><bold>limit.comp</bold> ×5  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>16×8  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><bold>Inflow limits</bold> ping-pong (<computeroutput>limitA</computeroutput>/<computeroutput>limitB</computeroutput>); how much each cell can accept.  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no" align='right'><para>9  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><bold>advect.comp</bold>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>16×8  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Move <bold>water/oil/lava</bold> along flux subject to limits; writes other cell buffer.  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no" align='right'><para>—  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>state ^= 1</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>—  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Toggle cell ping-pong after advection.  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no" align='right'><para>10  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><bold>separate.comp</bold> ×2  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>16×8, half height dispatch  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><bold>Phase separation</bold> oil/lava vs water on staggered rows; <computeroutput>operation[1]</computeroutput> checkerboard with <computeroutput>tick</computeroutput>.  </para>
</entry></row>
</table>
</para>
<para><bold>brush.comp</bold> (when painting): dispatches over a bounding box of the stroke; modes — deposit material/liquid, erase, or stir (<computeroutput>pc.operation</computeroutput> mode + <computeroutput>pc.brush</computeroutput> + radius).</para>
<para>This design is a <bold>bounded, real-time 2D fluid approximation</bold>: shared velocity, finite pressure iterations, finite-volume transport with donor/receiver limits — suited for gameplay rather than offline CFD accuracy.</para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="index_1rendering-path-graphics">
<title>Rendering path (graphics)</title><para><table rows="3" cols="3"><row>
<entry thead="yes"><para>Stage  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Shader  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Notes  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para>World  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><bold>fullscreen.vert</bold> + <bold>world.frag</bold>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Single large triangle; fragment shader maps canvas pixels → grid coords; includes <computeroutput>world.glsl</computeroutput> read-only. Shading: material/liquid reconstruction, absorption, highlights, Fresnel, refraction, lava glow, procedural noise.  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para>UI  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><bold>ui.vert</bold> + <bold>ui.frag</bold>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Instanced quads (<computeroutput>6</computeroutput> vertices × <computeroutput>quadCount</computeroutput>); per-quad bounds + RGBA from CPU <computeroutput>Quad</computeroutput> list. Bitmap font and panels drawn entirely on CPU in <computeroutput><ref refid="ui_8cpp_source" kindref="compound">ui.cpp</ref></computeroutput>.  </para>
</entry></row>
</table>
</para>
<para>Push constants for both passes share <computeroutput>canvas</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>cursor</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>screen</computeroutput> (and simulation uses the same layout block).</para>
<para>Pipeline: <bold>Vulkan dynamic rendering</bold> (no classic render pass object), swapchain format color attachment, scissor for world letterboxing.</para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="index_1shared-shader-library-worldglsl">
<title>Shared shader library (<computeroutput>world.glsl</computeroutput>)</title><para>Included by every <computeroutput>.comp</computeroutput> and by <computeroutput>world.frag</computeroutput> (with <computeroutput>WORLD_READ_ONLY</computeroutput>).</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><bold>Coordinate helpers</bold>: <computeroutput>inside</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>indexOf</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>readCell</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>writeCell</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>writeOther</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Material/thermo helpers</bold>: <computeroutput>packMatter</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>solid</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>wet</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>gas</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>faceWeight</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>inverseDensity</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>RNG</bold>: <computeroutput>hash32</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>random01</computeroutput> for stochastic grain motion.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Compute shaders use <computeroutput>#extension GL_GOOGLE_include_directive</computeroutput> and are compiled as Vulkan 1.3 SPIR-V.</para>
<para>Host code does not parse GLSL; keeping <computeroutput>Cell</computeroutput> layout and material IDs in sync is enforced by shared constants and static asserts in <computeroutput><ref refid="game_8hpp_source" kindref="compound">game.hpp</ref></computeroutput>.</para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="index_1testing-and-benchmarks">
<title>Testing and benchmarks</title><para><programlisting filename=".powershell"><codeline><highlight class="normal">.\build\Release\FallingSand.exe<sp/>--test<sp/>--validate</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">.\build\Release\FallingSand.exe<sp/>--window-test<sp/>--validate</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">.\build\Release\FallingSand.exe<sp/>--benchmark<sp/>1200<sp/>--scene<sp/>thermal</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><bold><computeroutput>--test</computeroutput></bold>: GPU checks (walls, divergence reduction, phase conservation, sand, thermal reactions, brush) without a visible window loop.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold><computeroutput>--window-test</computeroutput></bold>: Scene buttons, paint, step, resize, present, save/load.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold><computeroutput>--benchmark</computeroutput></bold>: 60-frame warmup, then mean/p95 GPU ms and simulation ms; device name in header.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><computeroutput>--validate</computeroutput> enables validation layers for debugging synchronization and API usage.</para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="index_1further-reading">
<title>Further reading</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Liquid solver inspiration: semi-Lagrangian advection, pressure projection, bounded Jacobi — see <ulink url="https://www.cs.ubc.ca/~rbridson/fluidsimulation/">Bridson &amp; Müller-Fischer, SIGGRAPH fluids course notes</ulink>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Swapchain synchronization: <ulink url="https://docs.vulkan.org/guide/latest/swapchain_semaphore_reuse.html">Khronos Vulkan Guide — swapchain semaphore reuse</ulink>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Shader authorship conventions in this repo: <computeroutput>STYLE.md</computeroutput> (optional reference for contributors).</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
</sect1>
